      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`RuntimeEndpoint.select` drops valid `0.0` logprobs because normalization filters by truthiness. A nonempty all-zero choice raises `ZeroDivisionError`; `[None, 0.0, -2.0]` is incorrectly averaged as `-2.0`, which can select the wrong choice.\n\nRefs #3509. This addresses the valid-zero residual only; empty/all-`None` ranking is unchanged.\n\n## Modifications\n\n### Summary\n\n```diff\n- if x[0]\n+ if x[0] is not None\n```\n\nKeep zero scores in the average while preserving `None` as the missing-value sentinel. Add registered CPU coverage for all-zero scores, mixed `None`/zero/negative scores, negative-score controls, and `token_length_normalized` ranking.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** the four new tests report three errors (zero division, wrong average, wrong choice); the negative-score control passes.\n- **After:** all four regression tests and the three original choice-policy tests pass.\n- Real localhost HTTP responses through the original `RuntimeEndpoint.select`: five cases pass, including token-healing and `None` controls (11 HTTP requests; no inference server or weights).\n- `pre-commit run --all-files`: all applicable hooks pass on the complete checkout, including registered-test checks and Rust hooks.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe deterministic choice-policy regressions and public endpoint protocol cases above validate the affected ranking. Valid zeros now participate in the mean. No model kernel/forward code changed; GPU model evaluation was not run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo inference performance change or speed claim; benchmarks were not run.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way. **Blast Radius:** frontend choice ranking with valid zero logprobs.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the contribution guide (`pre-commit run --all-files` passes).\n- [x] Add focused registered CPU unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation (no documented API change).\n- [ ] Provide model accuracy/speed benchmarks (not run; scope and deterministic validation described above).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\nHosted CI and maintainer review are pending. No CI labels or reruns have been requested.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and validation, submitted by the account owner’s authorized proxy.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39998337352](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39998337352)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39998337141](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39998337141)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39998337172](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39998337172)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
